\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces On the left, four selected non-disruptive shots incorrectly identified as disruptive by the CNN. Shots 176423 and 177030 feature a drop resembling a disruption, thereby confusing our model, while shot 178463 appears to be garbage data based off the current peaking at $\approx \qty {0.02}{\mega \ampere }$. On the right, four selected disruptive shots incorrectly identified as non-disruptive by the CNN. Each shot lacks the characteristic instant drop to zero that typically identifies a disruption. Shots 180501 and 177403 do not present an evident disruption and seem erroneously labeled.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cnn_errors}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
